// A UNIT variant constructed with `{ }`. The form test asks whether the variant
// is a tuple one, and a unit variant declares no fields at all - so the check
// returned early on "nothing to compare" and this walked past it.
//
// The reference calls a unit variant a TUPLE variant in this message, because
// struct-ness is a property it does not have. The wording is mirrored, not
// improved: a diagnostic that reads oddly and matches is worth more than one
// that reads well and diverges.
enum E { P(int) | Q }
fn main() { let e: E = E::Q { }; match e { E::P(x) => println(x) | E::Q => println(0) } }
